1785476327357490	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvEg		item.move	bn-1eo	{"state":"done"}	blake3:3MqcpHYXAfzWyUfPSRhBx8qSpjNiIEdWw21rwgd3rtE
1785476784822048	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvEw		item.update	bn-1mp	{"field":"description","value":"VERIFIED 2026-07-31, and the premise this was filed on was wrong. Everything\nbelow was measured against agy 1.1.8/1.1.9, not inferred.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG\n\nThe SQLite databases under ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/conversations/<uuid>.db are\nthe conversation *store*, not the transcript. Nothing needs to read them, and\nthe protobuf blobs inside them -- the whole reason this was sized l -- are not on\nthe path to observing agy at all.\n\nThe transcript is plain JSONL, one file per conversation:\n\n    ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/<conversationId>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\n\nIt exists for every conversation on this machine, including ones from 2026-07-21\nand 07-28, so it is written unconditionally and not gated on hooks being\nconfigured. `transcript_full.jsonl` sits beside it.\n\nRecord shape, which is friendlier than either agent already supported:\n\n    {\"step_index\": 2, \"source\": \"MODEL\", \"type\": \"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\n     \"status\": \"DONE\", \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T05:42:48Z\", \"content\": \"...\",\n     \"tool_calls\": [...], \"exit_code\": 0}\n\n`step_index` is a monotonic cursor, and `created_at` is exactly the ISO shape\niso_to_epoch already parses. tail.rs applies unchanged.\n\nVocabulary observed over a 148-record conversation:\n\n    USER_EXPLICIT / USER_INPUT          the prompt, and the turn start\n    MODEL / PLANNER_RESPONSE            assistant text\n    MODEL / RUN_COMMAND, VIEW_FILE,     tool calls, with tool_calls and\n                LIST_DIRECTORY          exit_code alongside\n    SYSTEM / CONVERSATION_HISTORY,      housekeeping, not a turn signal\n                CHECKPOINT, SYSTEM_MESSAGE\n\nHOOKS WORK, AND ARE CLAUDE-SHAPED\n\nagy reads hooks.json from a customization root -- ~/.agents/hooks.json is the\none that fired. Confirmed by probe: PreInvocation, PostInvocation and Stop all\nexecuted, each receiving JSON on stdin. They fire in interactive mode only; the\nsame config produced nothing under `agy -p`, which matters because print mode is\nnot what this observes anyway.\n\nEvents are PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PreInvocation, PostInvocation, Stop -- not\nSessionStart/UserPromptSubmit, so the register wiring is a different mapping\nfrom Claude's and Codex's, not a copy. Every payload carries the common fields\n(camelCase, protojson):\n\n    conversationId          the session id\n    workspacePaths          [cwd]\n    transcriptPath          the path above, MINUS the .jsonl extension\n    artifactDirectoryPath\n    modelName               e.g. gemini-3.6-flash-low\n\nStop additionally carries fullyIdle, executionNum, error and terminationReason\n(observed: NO_TOOL_CALL).\n\nSo the identity bridge is solved: conversationId and workspacePaths are exactly\nwhat `hook register` needs, and modelName arrives free.\n\nTHE ONE REAL PROBLEM: TURN END\n\nThere is no turn-end record in the transcript, and it is not derivable from one.\nThe obvious rule -- a PLANNER_RESPONSE with status DONE and no tool_calls, which\nis agy's own NO_TOOL_CALL termination reason -- was tested and fails: a 7-turn\nconversation yields 13 such records, because agy narrates between tool batches.\nInterleaving was UEUEEUEEEEUEEUEEUEUE. Any consumer built on that rule would\nclose turns early, several times per turn.\n\nThe Stop hook is therefore load-bearing, the same way Claude's turn_duration\nrecord is, and agy is the first host whose turn boundary arrives only by report.\n\nDESIGN, AND THE DECISION LEFT\n\nTranscript gives prompt, tools, model-side text, and timing. Stop gives the\nboundary. The join is where the choice is:\n\n  (a) Stop hook reports only the boundary, and the daemon attaches the running\n      answer it has been holding from PLANNER_RESPONSE records. Matches how\n      Claude's normaliser already works (turn.answer.take()), but the held\n      answer lives in a per-transcript Stream while inbox records are processed\n      on a separate path in main.rs, so it needs those two to meet.\n\n  (b) The Stop hook reads the last PLANNER_RESPONSE out of transcriptPath itself\n      and reports boundary and answer together, the way `hook subagent` already\n      passes last_assistant_message. Self-contained, no cross-path plumbing.\n      Blocked on ATOMIC_LIMIT: hook.rs silently drops any inbox line over 4096\n      bytes, so a long answer would vanish -- and vanish quietly, which is the\n      failure mode this codebase keeps getting bitten by.\n\n(b) is cleaner if the size limit is dealt with honestly: either the answer goes\nto a sidecar file the daemon reads, or that record type gets a different\ntransport. Do not simply raise ATOMIC_LIMIT -- it is what makes concurrent\nappends from several agents safe.\n\nWorth doing first regardless: register + prompt + tools + model, with no answer\ntext. That already gives working/idle and a labelled session, which is most of\nthe value, and it is small now that none of it involves protobuf.\n\nSize dropped l -> m: the expensive half was imaginary."}	blake3:hAmkEqWfPRs4VfdCwRLYos55H-6VTt63VEgbuoYPLgU
1785476784831917	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvFA		item.update	bn-1mp	{"field":"size","value":"m"}	blake3:GaEuYfDnp_iLZx_gIdHXkZWEkRQ3fXz-Bu-exEn88wI
1785476850622510	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvFQ		item.comment	bn-1f4	{"body":"Duplicate of bn-1eo — both were created by the same 'bn create' invocation running twice (the shell that filed it was spawned twice; the same accident command-substituted the backticked 'agentbus watch --session S' in the description and left a second observer running, which was corrupting events.jsonl until it was stopped). The work is implemented and verified under bn-1eo."}	blake3:x_sWNRXRDI0DwCbLT8Dj8JFfjRaoDn5OvrLnSZLx4jA
1785476850635364	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvFg		item.move	bn-1f4	{"state":"done"}	blake3:H_yzyEZFKV5OMM90ZtUup-pm0KkmLN6gnCtRs1oQmWc
1785514042233601	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvFw		item.comment	bn-1mp	{"body":"Implemented and verified end-to-end against a live agy guest: agentbus wait returned status=done in 1.4s with a 1024-char, 5-paragraph answer, and the session reads source=agy, state=idle, model=gemini-3.6-flash-low with its cwd and pid.\n\nOne correction to the description above: the hooks customization root is the WORKSPACE, not home. <workspace>/.agents/hooks.json fires; ~/.agents/hooks.json does not, and neither does ~/.gemini/.agents/hooks.json -- both were tried and neither ran. The earlier reading was wrong because a workspace hooks.json was still in place when the home one appeared to work. ~/.agents is a customization root for skills only. So 'just sync-agy [dir]' is per-project by necessity.\n\nAlso measured: agy does not expand a leading ~ in a hook command despite documenting that it does, and the failure is silent -- the hook simply never runs."}	blake3:-EaWMdFTiBaPzZ6AJSJ1qAI7DNN7UJCPFL6PZoN-0BY
1785514042246736	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvGA		item.move	bn-1mp	{"state":"done"}	blake3:dXTC0Q_NDxarkWoJ28ma39gYnxyRmbutFXAzr_5KiWU
1785515474035146	agentbus-dev	itc:v3:AWLJM_JJknJ8zQAAAAAAQdW_VauvtgAAAAEvGQ		item.comment	bn-1mp	{"body":"Correction to the earlier comment on hook location, now established by strace rather than by elimination: agy's global hooks file is ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json. It probes four paths — antigravity-cli/builtin/hooks.json, antigravity-cli/hooks.json, .gemini/hooks.json, .gemini/config/hooks.json — and opens the last. .agents/ is a customization root for skills and rules but is NOT read for hooks at any level, which is why both ~/.agents/hooks.json and a workspace .agents/hooks.json appeared to be the answer at different points and only one of them ever fired.\n\nThat makes 'just sync-agy' a one-time global install rather than per-project. Verified from two fresh directories with no .agents anywhere: agentbus wait returned done, and the session reads source=agy state=idle."}	blake3:v9XvEK5bBY8HyxbvqcWP2esnnNYndCRmaz3qjsnW-KI
